 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nIn the case of an error, the log of the service operation is filled with the corresponding error message.\n\nMessage Types\n\ne CreditManagementAccountERPPaymentBehaviourSummaryByDebtorPartyQuery_sync\n\ne CreditManagementAccountERPPaymentBehaviourSummaryByDebtorPartyResponse_sync\n\nNotes on SAP Implementation\n\nThe PropertyValuation is filled with key figures from the system in which Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable is running.\nConfiguration\n\ne Before you can use the service operation in Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable (FI-CA), you must activate the\nintegration with SAP Credit Management in Customizing forContract Accounts Receivable and Payable under Integration\n\n> Financial Supply Chain Management -> Credit Management -> Activate Credit Management .\n\ne If you want to transfer FI-CA key figures within the field PropertyValuation, you must activate the relevant key figures in\nCustomizing for Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable under Integration -> Financial Supply Chain Management ->\nCredit Management -> Key Figures -> Make Specifications for Key Figures for Credit Management .\n\nEnhancements\n\nEnhancements\n\nTo enhance the proxy structure of the current operation, you can use event 4614 (see the documentation of sample function\nmodule FKK_SAMPLE_4614).\n\nYou can create your own key figures and send them to the Credit Management system. For more information, see the Customizing\ndocumentation under Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable -> Integration > Financial Supply Chain Management ->\nCredit Management -> Key Figures -> Define Key Figures for Transfer to Credit Management .\n\nQuery Contract Account In\n\nDefinition\n\nRequest to contract account for provision of contract account data.\n\nTechnical Data\n\nEntity Type               Service Interface\nCategory                  A2X\n\nDirection         inbound\n",
